// What POST .../packaging would do, without doing it (PACK-001). Computed against the package as it
// stands, so it can change when a new version is saved in between; the packaging call checks again and
// is the one that decides.
// Ref: #/components/schemas/PackagingPreview
type PackagingPreview struct {
	Target PackagingTargetId `json:"target"`
	// Whether packaging would be permitted right now.
	Allowed bool `json:"allowed"`
	// Present exactly when `allowed` is false.
	BlockedReason OptPackagingBlockedReason `json:"blocked_reason"`
	// The reason in the user's language, safe to display as-is and served rather than assembled
	// client-side, so the preview and the 422 from the packaging call say the same sentence.
	BlockedMessage OptString         `json:"blocked_message"`
	Validation     PackageValidation `json:"validation"`
	// What the package needs installed, as the download page's half of 02:PACK-002 第 1 條. These are
	// the exact lines the produced INSTALL.md carries, from the same `skillpkg` findings, so the page and
	// the packaged document cannot disagree about what a Skill needs.
	//
	// It includes the dependencies the package never declares but its scripts import
	// (`undeclared-dependency`): that is the first reason a reader follows the instructions and the Skill
	// still does not run.
	//
	// Empty when a licensing gate closed before any bytes were read — there is no package yet to have
	// dependencies — and empty when the package genuinely declares and imports nothing. The preview's
	// `allowed` and `blocked_reason` tell those two apart.
	Dependencies []string `json:"dependencies"`
	// The test cases that would travel in the package (PACK-005). Empty when the caller did not ask for
	// them, and empty is not the same as "there are none" — `excluded_test_cases` says which were left
	// out and why.
	IncludedTestCases []PackagingPreviewIncludedTestCasesItem `json:"included_test_cases"`
	// Test cases that will not travel, each with its reason. Listed rather than omitted so the user is
	// told what they are not getting — most often that a dataset they uploaded cannot be redistributed,
	// which is a decision about licensing and not a defect in their test case.
	ExcludedTestCases []PackagingPreviewExcludedTestCasesItem `json:"excluded_test_cases"`
	// Source files the packager removed, each with its reason.
	//
	// The exporter has always dropped these — `.git/`, `node_modules/`, `.ssh/`, `.env`, symlinks —
	// and until now it dropped them silently: nothing in the manifest, nothing on this page, nothing in
	// INSTALL.md. `excluded_test_cases` existed for exactly this reason one field over, and the argument
	// is the same one 02:PACK-001 makes about keeping the Skill's directory structure: a package missing a
	// file the Skill needs is not the same product as one that never had it, and only one of those two is
	// worth telling the author about.
	//
	// Empty for almost every package. It is not empty for the case that matters — a Skill that vendored
	// its dependencies, or one whose `SKILL.md` points at something the exporter would not carry.
	ExcludedFiles []PackagingPreviewExcludedFilesItem `json:"excluded_files"`
	// How long the package this preview describes would be kept, in whole days, before the platform
	// deletes it (03:PACK-011).
	//
	// On the preview and not on the packaging response, on purpose. 02:NFR-001 asks that a limit which
	// will affect the user be visible before they hit it - the same reasoning that put `redistribution` on
	// the owner's list - and the packaging response arrives after the decision it would be informing. It
	// is not on GET /packaging/targets either: retention is one deployment number, not a property of a
	// target, and three targets would put three copies of it on the wire.
	//
	// It is the value the create call writes into the artifact's `expires_at`, read from the same
	// `DOWNLOAD_ARTIFACT_RETENTION` the deployment configures. Clients render this number and never a
	// constant of their own (設計 §2.2 顯示與強制成對).
	//
	// Required, because a deployment with no ratified period answers 503 for this whole endpoint rather
	// than serving a preview with an unknown one: no ratified number, no number on the screen, and no
	// build either. Truncated rather than rounded - the value is a promise about how long the bytes
	// survive, so the error falls on the side of promising less. A deployment configured shorter than a
	// day answers 0, which 02:NFR-002a 第 1 條 already forbids.
	RetentionDays int `json:"retention_days"`
}

